                                   "The student’s or spouse/common-law partner’s children are permanently disabled, are 19 years of age or over, are fully supported by the student or spouse/common-law partner and are claimed on the student’s or spouse/common-law partner’s income tax return; or the children are the student’s foster children and foster-parent income is claimed on the application." ,
                                   "a dependant is defined as a wholly dependent person who resides with the borrower (or is in a healthcare facility) and is either under 18 years of age; or 18 and over and dependent by reason of a mental or physical infirmity and has been claimed and approved by the Canada Revenue Agency as wholly dependent for tax purposes." ;
                   prov:wasDerivedFrom data:CAN_UNIT_00413 ,
