###  https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/uk#DefinedTerm
gro-uk:DefinedTerm rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf cco:Resource ,
                                   cco:Role ;
                   rdfs:label "Costs Definition" ,
                              "Defined Term" ,
                              "Fees Retained and Charges Definition" ,
                              "Main providers and employer-providers" ,
                              "Mentoring" ;
                   skos:definition "Costs include any co-investment or additional training and assessment costs above the funding band, that the employer has paid directly to the provider, where this is part of the agreed apprenticeship." ,
                                   "Main providers and employer-providers receiving funding for delivering apprenticeship training and on-programme assessment in England" ,
                                   "Mentoring must meet the definition of off-the-job training (new learning, relevant to the apprenticeship, not English and maths, delivered within normal working hours) and be documented in the training plan. The mentor must be a more senior or experienced member of staff. This does not include general line management. The apprentice must not be doing productive work." ,
                                   "The full range of fees retained by the provider and charges (which must be eligible costs) that apply, including funding retained for managing quality assurance / oversight and for administrative functions such as data returns." ,
                                   "These rules form part of the terms and conditions for the use of funds in an employer’s apprenticeship service account or for government-employer co-investment." ;
                   prov:wasDerivedFrom data:UK_UNIT_00005 ,
                                       data:UK_UNIT_00013 ,
                                       data:UK_UNIT_00715 ,
